      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 609264196,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This would mean that only CAN frames coming in this way (Socket CAN) would hit these new sub dissector tables.\n\nWhat about the others?\n* packet-tecmp.c\n* packet-ieee1722.c\n* packet-caneth.c\n\nShould we change this for all at the same time?\n\nCurrently all dissectors that can carry CAN frames look for the SocketCAN sub dissector tables and based on their local \"heuristics first\" variable, write code like this:\nhttps://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-tecmp.c#L1134\n\nCreating a common function instead of doing the same in each of these seems to be cleaner. While the \"heuristics_first\" variable needs to stay inside each, would it be possible to push the if statements that would need to be extended in this case to the packet-socketcan.c and export a function similar to this:\ngboolean hand_can_frame_to_subdissectors(tvbuff_t *tvb, packet_info *pinfo, proto_tree *tree, const gboolean add_proto_name, struct can_info *data, const gboolean heuristics_first)\n\nI can help.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6878858,
            "username": "LarsVoelker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dr. Lars Völker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/cccf2084a0438673e9e09f07ed0a5035f6e8815d3d5d888db0023a757c8dce8c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/LarsVoelker"
          },
